Components that restrict how this stack can be used or distributed
-------------------------------------------------------------------
These four matter. Read them before you publish an image or use anything commercially.

1. ultralytics (AGPL-3.0)
   Used by TWO services: stack/vision (ultralytics==8.4.145, YOLO26n) and
   stack/advanced_live_portrait (ultralytics==8.2.0 in its Dockerfile). Building,
   distributing or network-serving either service takes on AGPL-3.0 obligations. Weights
   distributed with ultralytics carry the same terms. See stack/vision/AGPL_NOTICE.md.

2. InsightFace buffalo_l model pack (non-commercial research use only)
   The Advanced LivePortrait path loads `insightface.app.FaceAnalysis(name='buffalo_l')`
   (LivePortrait/utils/face_analysis_diy.py upstream). InsightFace's code is MIT, but its
   README states that models trained on its data "are available for non-commercial research
   purposes only" and that buffalo_l requires contacting them for licensing. The LivePortrait
   weights bundle ships an `insightface` directory. Treat the LivePortrait/ALP path as
   research-use-only.

3. ComfyUI-AdvancedLivePortrait (NO LICENSE)
   github.com/PowerHouseMan/ComfyUI-AdvancedLivePortrait has no license file (GitHub reports
   none; last push 2024-08-21). Without a license, all rights are reserved by default. This
   repository does not contain that code: the Dockerfile fetches a pinned commit at build time.
   Do not publish an image containing it. UNRESOLVED: ask the author for a license.

4. LFM2.5-VL-450M / 3B (LFM 1.0 license, not an OSS license)
   Model card license: "other / lfm1.0". Read it before use. Not included.

